.claude/

# The canonical daily log and its plain-text export. Strategy owns the .docx; the
# .txt exists so the coding lane can READ it without a shell. Both are a working
# exchange between lanes — NOT platform content.
#
# Never committed, for two reasons. `publish = "."` in netlify.toml makes the repo
# root the public web root (#99), so a tracked copy would serve both lanes' full
# history at a guessable URL. And keeping them untracked means `git status` stays
# clean, so an accidental `git add .` cannot pick them up.
#
# Both live in docs/ alongside docs/daily-log/, which IS committed — the day entries
# the coding lane writes are platform-adjacent record; the canonical log is not.
#
# Re-export the .txt whenever the .docx is merged: File → Save As → Plain Text,
# into docs/, same filename. Nothing else to do.
#
# No leading slash on these patterns, so they match at any depth — moving the files
# to another folder does not un-ignore them.
VeyaFlow_Daily_Log.docx
VeyaFlow_Daily_Log.txt
